coordinated home systems. The same infrastructure approach now moves to another part of the charging network that directly serves drivers. Tesla Superchargers across Massachusetts open to compatible vehicles from other manufacturers. Additional locations statewide now accept non-Tesla electric cars as part of the continued open access effort. The change increases available stations for owners already on the road without new construction.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:24.980
That expansion on existing hardware leads into refinements taking place on the production line itself. Recent cyber truck deliveries show updated side-repeater cameras without any model-year designation. A self-reinforcing polypropylene arrow shield also appears on the same vehicles. The shield reduces cost while improving reliability and assembly speed. Tesla continues to introduce these component upgrades as soon as they clear testing.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:43.620
Those hardware adjustments connect to a separate cabin technology project that improves the listening experience. Tesla and Princeton developed a system that measures cabin acoustics and aligns individual speakers. Frequency dependent filters are then applied after arrival times and levels are recorded near the listeners.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:02:06.800
Late high-frequency reflections stay uncorrected so natural distance cues remain intact. Cabin cameras track head position and allow the filters to switch in real time. The method reduces processing demands while keeping the sound stage stable for multiple occupants. That work on cabin sound follows a first principles approach to handling reflections rather than eliminating them.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:18.340
Vehicle interiors create complex echo patterns that most systems try to remove entirely. The new method instead measures actual impulse responses and decides which arrivals to correct.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:36.420
Correction windows narrow at higher frequencies so late reflections can still serve as distance cues. Separate band limited solutions for tweeters and woofers are recombined with linked with Riley crossovers. Short filters lower power consumption and stay stable when listeners shift position.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:44.400
The same occupant sensors already installed in the vehicle now support audio adaptation with almost no added cost.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:59.460
